A candidate factor is therefore retained only when
all four criteria jointly hold.
C
Evaluation Metrics
We evaluate the time-series performance of the
resulting trading strategies using standard portfolio-
level performance metrics. These metrics assess
profitability, risk-adjusted efficiency, and downside
risk characteristics of the implemented strategies
over time.
C.1
Annualized Return (AR)
Let Rp
t and Rb
t denote the portfolio and benchmark
returns at period t, and define the active return
At = Rp
t −Rb
t. Let N be the number of trading
periods per year.
The annualized excess return is defined as
AR =
