The remaining trading-strategy environment is
shared by FaVOR and every baseline. Data splits,
transaction costs, Qlib execution rule, and stop-loss
policy are applied identically across all methods.
Each baseline model is trained and tuned using the
Qlib (Yang et al., 2020) reference workflow config-
uration without modification. This covers the input
feature set, label horizon, training objective, hyper-
parameter search budget, validation usage, and ran-
dom seed handling. For the ML and DL baselines
the input feature set is Alpha158 (Microsoft, 2025),
and the same feature set is provided to FaVOR and
the LLM-based baselines as the underlying observ-
able column set. Table 9 summarizes this shared
backtest environment.
